{
  "_comment": [
    "Sandbox profile for the H1 QA triage agent (CC-AGENTS-DESIGN §4, ported",
    "from the helm recipe). The agent READS artifacts and WRITES prose. It",
    "executes nothing: the deterministic runner (experiments/nightly.py) owns",
    "execution, so jobs stay reproducible and exit-coded whether cron, a human",
    "or an agent triggers them (acceptance criterion 1).",
    "",
    "Denying interpreters is what makes the split structural rather than a",
    "promise: an agent that cannot run python cannot quietly re-run a job,",
    "re-grade an answer, or edit an oracle (criterion 5).",
    "",
    "Usage:",
    "  claude -p --settings qa/triage-settings.json \\",
    "         --append-system-prompt \"$(cat qa/triage-prompt.md)\" \\",
    "         --output-format stream-json --verbose --max-turns 40 \\",
    "         'Triage last night's run.'"
  ],
  "permissions": {
    "defaultMode": "acceptEdits",
    "allow": [
      "Read(.qa-artifacts/reports/**)",
      "Read(.qa-artifacts/runs/**)",
      "Read(.qa-artifacts/truth/**)",
      "Read(experiments/runs/**)",
      "Read(experiments/golden/**)",
      "Read(docs/**)",
      "Read(experiments/*.py)",
      "Read(x1_advisor/**)",
      "Write(.qa-artifacts/reports/**)",
      "Edit(.qa-artifacts/reports/**)",
      "Bash(git log:*)",
      "Bash(git show:*)",
      "Bash(git diff:*)",
      "Bash(ls:*)",
      "Bash(jq:*)"
    ],
    "deny": [
      "Read(./.env)",
      "Read(./.env.*)",
      "Read(**/.env)",
      "Read(**/credentials*)",
      "Read(**/*service-account*)",
      "Read(~/.config/gcloud/**)",
      "Bash(cat .env*)",
      "Bash(env)",
      "Bash(printenv)",
      "Bash(python*)",
      "Bash(python3*)",
      "Bash(uv*)",
      "Bash(pytest*)",
      "Bash(psql*)",
      "Bash(curl*)",
      "Bash(wget*)",
      "Bash(nc*)",
      "Bash(ssh*)",
      "Bash(git commit:*)",
      "Bash(git push:*)",
      "Bash(git add:*)",
      "Bash(gcloud*)",
      "Bash(cloud-sql-proxy*)",
      "Write(experiments/**)",
      "Write(x1_advisor/**)",
      "Write(docs/**)",
      "Write(tests/**)",
      "Edit(experiments/**)",
      "Edit(x1_advisor/**)",
      "Edit(docs/**)",
      "Edit(tests/**)",
      "Write(.qa-artifacts/truth/**)",
      "Edit(.qa-artifacts/truth/**)"
    ]
  },
  "env": {
    "ADVISOR_QA_EXPORT": "0"
  }
}
